# The disk of `tests/run stress` and `stress-ahci`: stressprobe on a KRFFS
# root on disk.
#
# mkdisk.sh builds it, and the suite boots it with rach2.fsdisk and
# rach2.rescue. The debug shell runs `exec /stressprobe`, which writes 33 MiB
# of files and reads them back through a page cache of at most 8 MiB, so that
# the data that comes back has been through the disk.
file 0755 /stressprobe build/tests/stressprobe
